    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "No, but I’d imagine tools like Khan Academy’s adaptive quizzes or chatbots for step-by-step explanations could be great for learners. Since my education ended with a vocational diploma, I never had such tech, but hypothetically, AI might bridge gaps by offering personalized practice—something low conscientiousness (work-driven) might appreciate for breaking tasks into smaller parts.",
